# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build / environment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.venv-*/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.env
*.env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data and experimental output — never versioned
#
# Corpora are rebuilt from source (scripts/download_fold_a.py) and run
# directories are large, machine-specific, and immutable by design. Results get
# published deliberately, not by accident of `git add -A`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/
artifacts/
*.npy
*.npz
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent working files — reviews, briefs, cross-model conversation logs
#
# The working record of how the analysis was produced. Useful locally; not a
# publication artifact.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/
docs/build_log.md
docs/codex_review*.md
docs/review_brief*.md
docs/corrections_*.md
docs/theory_panel_*.md
docs/research_audit_*.md
docs/colab_readiness_audit.md
claude_code_setup.md
project_instructions.md
decisions_log.md
cliffguard-unified-paper.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local results — held back until the Colab run completes and results are
# published deliberately.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/results_*.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private manuscripts
#
# docs/paper/main.tex, refs.bib and figures/ stay tracked because the
# figure-generation workflow depends on them. Draft proposals and compiled PDFs
# do not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/paper/proposal.tex
docs/paper/*roposal*.pdf
docs/paper/*urposal*.pdf
docs/paper/*.aux
docs/paper/*.out
docs/paper/*.synctex.gz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch and logs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
scratchpad/
tmp/
*.log
external_data/

# Downloaded run archives and their extractions
notebooks/cliffguard_colab_*/
notebooks/cliffguard_colab_*.zip
notebooks/colab_alreadyrun.ipynb

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notebook noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb_checkpoints
notebooks/.ipynb_checkpoints/
notebooks/I_DID/
notebooks/.env

# Agent workflow documents
development.md

# Superseded bibliography: entries were unverifiable
docs/paper/refs.bib

# Council/agent review output
docs/council_review.md

# LaTeX build products. The .tex, .bib, generated figures and tables are
# tracked; anything a compile regenerates is not. The compiled PDF is added
# explicitly when a version is meant to be shared.
docs/paper/*.aux
docs/paper/*.bbl
docs/paper/*.blg
docs/paper/*.fdb_latexmk
docs/paper/*.fls
docs/paper/*.log
docs/paper/*.out
docs/paper/*.toc

# Private documents: the proposal and its build are the author's, not part of
# the paper release. These have twice been swept in by a broad `git add`.
docs/paper/*proposal*
docs/paper/*Proposal*
docs/paper/proposal.tex

# Superseded drafts and their figures. The released paper is
# docs/paper/cliff_artifact.tex; anything that was an earlier route to it is
# kept locally and not published.
docs/paper/main.tex
docs/paper/figures/generate_figures.py
docs/paper/figures/fig_decoupling.*
docs/paper/figures/fig_metrics.*
docs/paper/figures/fig_normalized.*
docs/paper/figures/fig_pipeline.*
docs/paper/figures/fig_scheme_progression.*
docs/paper/figures/fig_thresholds.*

# Superseded planning and theory documents. These describe the earlier
# defense-system and rate-distortion direction, whose headline claims did not
# survive measurement. Kept locally for provenance; not part of the release.
docs/theorems.md
docs/math.md
docs/pivot_plan_2026-08.md
docs/preregistration.md
docs/cliffguard_complete_guide.md
docs/what_is_it.md
